{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Nejatimoharrami, Farzad","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384324"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robotic automation to augment quality of artificial chemical life experiments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://mitpress.mit.edu/sites/default/files/titles/free_download/9780262339360_ALIFE_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384324","identifier":[{"id":"85087106333","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d05519fb-36c3-4664-86ac-dd6a107433d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-38EA4606F8BC7B5D557646FCB1CFAFFF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://mitpress.mit.edu/sites/default/files/titles/free_download/9780262339360_ALIFE_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Farzad","key":"nejatimoharramipau","last":"Nejatimoharrami","name":"Nejatimoharrami, Farzad","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780262339360"],"pages":"634-635","publisher":"MIT Press","series":"Complex Adaptive Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Artificial Life Conference 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087106333"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d05519fb-36c3-4664-86ac-dd6a107433d6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Robotic Automation to Augment Quality of Artificial Chemical Life Experiments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384324","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Liquid handling robots are rarely used in the domain of artificial life. In this field, transitory behaviours of non-equilibrium man-made systems are studied and need an automatic monitoring and logging of results. In addition, artificial life experiments are dynamic with frequent changes, which makes it difficult to apply conventional liquid handling robots as they are designed to automate a predefined task. In order to address these issues, we have developed an open source liquid handling robot, EvoBot. It uses a modular approach, which gives us the possibility to reconfigure the robot for different experiments and make it possible for users to add functionality by just developing a function specific module. In addition, it provides sensors and extra functionality for monitoring an experiment, which allows researchers to perform interactive experiments with the aim of prolonging non-equilibrium conditions. In this paper, we describe the modular design of EvoBot, document its performance, and provide a novel example of an interactive experiment in artificial life, where the robot nurtures a microbial fuel cell based on its voltage output.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Faina, Andres","Nejatimoharrami, Farzad","Støy, Kasper","Theodosiou, Pavlina","Taylor, Benjamin","Ieropoulos, Ioannis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381508"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-08","place":"Cancun, mx","start":"2016-07-04","title":"Artificial Life","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of the West of England"],"keyword":["Artificial Life","Liquid handling robots","Microbial fuel cell experimentation","Modular robotics","Non equilibrium systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evobot an open source modular liquid handling robot for nurturing microbial fuel cells","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81147673/faina2016alife_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381508","identifier":[{"id":"85087104378","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-10351349-c4af-4865-8965-d317fddbf1f6"],"keyword":["Artificial life","Liquid handling robots","Microbial fuel cell experimentation","Modular robotics","Non-equilibrium systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-9C457B591F8F520797824381A6C7DDE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81147673/faina2016alife_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of the west of england","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of the West of England","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Farzad","key":"nejatimoharramipau","last":"Nejatimoharrami","name":"Nejatimoharrami, Farzad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"fi