{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Janská, Petra","Zadražil, Aleš","Nejatimoharrami, Farzad","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper","Čejková, Jitka"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383097"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-27","place":"Tatranské Matliare, sk","start":"2016-05-23","title":"43rd Conference of Slovak Society of Chemical Engineering","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Czechia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Chemistry and Technology Prague"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collective behaviour in droplet systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383097","ids":["itu-7cbfc7ef-81e0-4fee-94c8-3f67d37549b0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BED6284AE818CBDDDA1711EB61456045"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cz","key":"university of chemistry and technology prague","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Chemistry and Technology Prague","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Petra","key":"janskápau","last":"Janská","name":"Janská, Petra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleš","key":"zadražilpau","last":"Zadražil","name":"Zadražil, Aleš","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Farzad","key":"nejatimoharramipau","last":"Nejatimoharrami","name":"Nejatimoharrami, Farzad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jitka","key":"čejkovápau","last":"Čejková","name":"Čejková, Jitka","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7cbfc7ef-81e0-4fee-94c8-3f67d37549b0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Collective behaviour in droplet systems","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383097","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Due to the replacement of natural flora and fauna with ur- ban environments, a significant part of the earth’s organisms that function as primary consumers have been dispelled. To compensate for the reduction in the amount of primary con- sumers, robotic systems that mimic plant-like organisms are interesting to mimic for their potential functional and aes- thetic value in urban environments. To investigate how to utilize plant developmental strategies in order to engender ur- ban artificial plants, we built a simple evolutionary model that applies an L-System based grammar as an abstraction of plant development. In the presented experiments, phytomorpholo- gies (plant morphologies) are iteratively constructed using a context sensitive L-System. The genomic representation of the L-System is subject to mutation by an evolutionary al- gorithm. These mutations thus alter the developmental rules of these phytomorphologies. We compare the differences be- tween the light absorption of evolving virtual plants that re- main static during their life and virtual plants that possess the possibility to move joints that link the separate parts of the virtual plants. Our results show that our evolutionary al- gorithm did not exploit potential beneficial joint actuation, instead, mostly static structures evolved. The results of our evolving L-System show that it is able to create various phy- tomorphologies, albeit that the results are preliminary and will be more thoroughly investigated in the future","author_count":4,"contributors":["Veenstra, Frank","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382007"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-08","place":"Cancun, mx","start":"2016-07-04","title":"Artificial Life","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary Robotics","L Systems","Plant Inspired Robotics","Simulated Evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generating artificial plant morphologies for function and aesthetics through evolving l systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81213335/Eventual_article_Plant.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382007","identifier":[{"id":"85087106895","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-32dfa560-6838-4b38-8c1f-ccd0a0fcb432"],"keyword":["Evolutionary Robotics","L-Systems","Plant-Inspired Robotics","Simulated Evolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-496139302AC1F596981041A15F298CCB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81213335/Eventual_article_Plant.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9780262339360"],"pages":"692-699","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Artificial Life Conference 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087106895"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-32dfa560-6838-4b38-8c1f-ccd0a0fcb432"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Generating Artificial Plant Morphologies for Function and Aesthetics through Evolving L-Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382007","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Veenstra, Frank","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382025"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-07","place":"Laubusch, de","start":"2015-10-05","title":"Workshop on \"Methods for Self-Organizing Distributed Systems\"","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving self organizing simulated plant inspired robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382025","ids":["itu-33b11ae2-1485-4b88-93c0-e28bed2e1f98"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C23D9487116FAB941EA7A22BCEA7582D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-33b11ae2-1485-4b88-93c0-e28bed2e1f98"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving self-organizing simulated plant-inspired robots","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382025","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Self-reconfigurable robots are built from robotic modules typically organised in a lattice. The robotic modules themselves are complete, although simple, robots and have onboard batteries, actuators, sensors, processing power, and communication capabilities. The modules can automatically connect to and disconnect from neighbour modules and move around in the lattice of modules. The self-reconfigurable robot as a whole can, through this automatic rearrangement of modules, change its own shape to adapt to the environment or as a response to new tasks. Potential advantages of self-reconfigurable robots are extreme versatility and robustness. The organisation of self-reconfigurable robots in a lattice structure and the emphasis on local communication between modules mean that lattice automata are a useful basis for control of self-reconfigurable robots. However, there are significant differences which arise mainly from the physical nature of self-reconfigurable robots as opposed to the virtual nature of lattice automata. The problems resulting from these differences are mutual exclusion, handling motion constraints of modules, and unrealistic assumption about global, spatial orientation. Despite these problems the self-reconfigurable robot community has successfully applied lattice automata to simple control problems. However, for more complex problems hybrid solutions based on lattice automata and distributed algorithms are used. Hence, lattice automata have shown to have potential for the control of self-reconfigurable robots, but still a unifying implementation based on lattice automata solving a complex control problem running on physical self-reconfigurable robot is yet to be demonstrated.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382685"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Control systems","Distributed algorithms","Lattice automata","Robotic modules","Self reconfigurable robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lattice automata for control of self reconfigurable robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382685","ids":["itu-5e799b78-8afa-4254-99c5-3d34fb40ea77"],"keyword":["Control systems","Distributed algorithms","Lattice automata","Robotic modules","Self-reconfigurable robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-60F7C3932936B409F6CB854B4186C336"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Georgios","key":"sirakoulispedh","last":"Sirakoulis","name":"Sirakoulis, Georgios","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew","key":"adamatzkypedh","last":"Adamatzky","name":"Adamatzky, Andrew","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-10924-4_2","edition":"1","eisbn":["9783319109244"],"isbn":["9783319109237"],"issn":["21947287"],"pages":"33-45","publisher":"Springer","series":"Emergence, Complexity, and Computation","status":"p","title":"Robots and Lattice Automata","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5e799b78-8afa-4254-99c5-3d34fb40ea77"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lattice Automata for Control of Self-Reconfigurable Robots","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382685","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Besides the life-as-it-could-be driver of artificial life research there is also the concept of extending natural life by creating hybrids or mixed societies that are built from natural and artificial components. In this paper we motivate and present the research program of the project flora robotica. Our objective is to develop and to investigate closely linked symbiotic relationships between robots and natural plants and to explore the potentials of a plant-robot society able to produce architectural artifacts and living spaces. These robot-plant bio-hybrids create synergies that allow for new functions of plants and robots. They also create novel design opportunities for an architecture that fuses the design and construction phase. The bio-hybrid is an example of mixed societies between ‘hard artificial and ‘wet natural life, which enables an interaction between natural and artificial ecologies. They form an embodied, self-organizing, and distributed cognitive system which is supposed to grow and develop over long periods of time resulting in the creation of meaningful architectural structures. A key idea is to assign equal roles to robots and plants in order to create a highly integrated, symbiotic system. Besides the gain of knowledge, this project has the objective to create a bio-hybrid system with a defined function and application – growing architectural artifacts.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hamann, Heiko","Wahby, Mostafa","Schmickl, Thomas","Zahadat, Payam","Hofstadler, Daniel","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian","Faina, Andres","Veenstra, Frank","Kernbach, Serge","Kuksin, Igor","Kernbach, Olga","Ayers, Phil","Wojtaszek, Przemyslaw"],"cuid":["S02-089.67-012432"],"event":{"acronym":"IEEE SSCI","end":"2015-12-10","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2015-12-07","title":"2015 IEEE Symposium on Artifical Life","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Poland"],"glorg":["Adam Mickiewicz University","All Global Affiliations","Cybertronica UG (Haftungsbeschrankt)","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"keyword":["Architecture","Artificial Life","Bio hybrid","Bio hybrid systems","Plants","Robots","Self organizing systems","architectural artifacts","plant robot symbiosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flora robotica mixed societies of symbiotic robot plant bio hybrids","src":["arkc","itu"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SSCI.2015.158","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.67-012432","identifier":[{"id":"84964937762","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-8a5ce1d1-e2e0-4c7d-9e51-2001d8744f9a","itu-4181dddd-1be3-4361-8109-ca1419e73d88"],"keyword":["Architecture","Bio-hybrid","No","Plants","Robots","architectural artifacts","artificial life","bio-hybrid systems","plant-robot symbiosis","self-organizing systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB54DC9B986B7E29B1E706A371F1092E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80993764/IEEE_ALIFE_2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SSCI.2015.158","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"it