{"abstract":"We explore vacuum as bonding force for modular robotics. Vacuubes are a set of modules that propagate vacuum across their interfaces in order to generate adhesive forces to form and hold structures. We use analog circuits to simulate vacuum transients and understand critical design parameters and then validate these insights in experiments. A 49-module structure that employs vacuum bonding is demonstrated. We conclude that vacuum offers a relatively strong, simple, reliable, and power-efficient connection principle.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Garcia, Ricardo Franco Mendoza","Hiller, J.D.","Støy, Kasper","Lipson, Hod"],"cuid":["S02-087.50-038286"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University"],"keyword":["Cellular and modular robots","Mechanism design","vacuum connectors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a vacuum based bonding mechanism for modular robotics","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/80053642950","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-087.50-038286","identifier":[{"id":"80053642950","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3b3af7bc-daa1-40b0-a225-956b9fe0b08f","sdu-50144acd-333f-4867-a34a-ea130206cb0b"],"keyword":["Cellular and modular robots","mechanism design","vacuum connectors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1EB91E21CB94D6895144A13D43AB8F1E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ricardo Franco Mendoza","key":"garciapau","last":"Garcia","locid":"d9da2d2d-b410-4092-974d-943a2cad1d97","name":"Garcia, Ricardo Franco Mendoza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.D.","key":"hillerpau","last":"Hiller","name":"Hiller, J.D.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"dab546c1-7862-404d-b783-4bdb8a321d52","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hod","key":"lipsonpau","last":"Lipson","name":"Lipson, Hod","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15523098","19410468"],"issn_org":["15523098"],"issue":"5","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Robotics","pages":"876-890","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Robotics","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Robotics","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80053642950"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3b3af7bc-daa1-40b0-a225-956b9fe0b08f","sdu-50144acd-333f-4867-a34a-ea130206cb0b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A vacuum-based bonding mechanism for modular robotics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.50-038286","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Producing steady stable and energy efficient locomotion in legged robots with the ability to walk in unknown terrain is a big challenge in robotics. In addressing this challenge, it is often desirable to experiment with different morphologies and see how they influence on the way the robot walks. This is however not always easy, since robots are often built as a fixed system with a limited possibility of changing the morphology without redesign a significant part of the robot. This work is focusing on the creation of a robotic construction kit specifically aimed at easing the process of constructing legged robots. This is accomplished by giving the creator the possibility to easily do morphological changes to the robot even after it have been build, to see how it effects the robot’s ability to walk in unknown terrain.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Jørgen Christian","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038420"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Energy efficient locomotion","Legged robots","Morphology","Robotic construction kit","Unknown terrain"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"locokit a construction kit for exploration of morphology of legged robots","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/53143130/CFP2011_Preamble.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-100.00-038420","ids":["itu-fe9dafdd-2036-4a19-9ebc-1e92129d3456","sdu-dbb6daf2-ade3-43e4-b2c2-c95d6e4f7764"],"keyword":["Energy-efficient locomotion","Legged robots","Morphology","Robotic construction kit","Unknown terrain"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-A888F4A7EE769DE01106810B239434A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/53143130/CFP2011_Preamble.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen Christian","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7360ab40-7502-495e-9745-33ad27e0e1cd","name":"Larsen, Jørgen Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-4741-8290","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"dab546c1-7862-404d-b783-4bdb8a321d52","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fe9dafdd-2036-4a19-9ebc-1e92129d3456","sdu-dbb6daf2-ade3-43e4-b2c2-c95d6e4f7764"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"LocoKit - A Construction Kit for Exploration of Morphology of Legged Robots","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038420","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Modular, self-reconfigurable robots are robotic systems that can change their own shape by autonomously rearranging the physical modules from which they are built. In this work, we are interested in how to distributedly execute a specified self-reconfiguration sequence. The sequence is specified using a simple and centralized scripting language, which either could be the outcome of a planner or be hand-coded. The distributed controller generated from this language allows for parallel self-reconfiguration steps and is highly robust to communication errors and loss of local state due to software failures. Furthermore, the self-reconfiguration sequence can automatically be reversed, if desired. We verify our approach and demonstrate its robustness in experiments using physical and the simulated ATRON modules, as well as simulated M-TRAN modules. Overall, the contribution of this work is the combination of the tractability of a centralized scripting language with the robustness and parallelism of distributed controllers in modular robots.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schultz, Ulrik Pagh","Bordignon, Mirko","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S02-096.97-038415"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Control of Robotic Systems","Modular Robots","Robotic Self Diagnosis and Self Repair","Robotic Self Replication","Sensor Networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robust and reversible execution of self reconfiguration sequences","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/79951802712","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.97-038415","identifier":[{"id":"79951802712","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f969d546-46e9-4bb3-bd6f-5c1fc28ef429","sdu-1d8d25b5-1719-4bc7-8a1f-9f2d69f313a5"],"keyword":["Control of Robotic Systems","Modular Robots","Robotic Self-Diagnosis and Self-Repair","Robotic Self-Replication","Sensor Networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FE01C80151F3D1C724C77E3DCA2C2AB9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Pagh","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","locid":"79a07bec-ac88-404c-8d6b-c9180214bcc6","name":"Schultz, Ulrik Pagh","orcid":"0000-0003-4119-2689","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mirko","key":"bordignonpau","last":"Bordignon","locid":"fc357837-c0e4-44fb-a4bb-63316c2d39ae","name":"Bordignon, Mirko","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"dab546c1-7862-404d-b783-4bdb8a321d52","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["02635747","14698668"],"issn_org":["02635747"],"journal":"Robotica","pages":"35-57","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Robotica","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79951802712"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f969d546-46e9-4bb3-bd6f-5c1fc28ef429","sdu-1d8d25b5-1719-4bc7-8a1f-9f2d69f313a5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Robust and reversible execution of self-reconfiguration sequences","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.97-038415","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The task of producing steady, stable and energy efficient locomotion in legged robots with the ability to walk in un- known terrain have for many years been a big challenge in robotics. This work is focusing on how different robots build from the modular robotic system, LocoKit by Larsen et. la [3], performs compared to animals, and also on the similari- ties between robots an animals. This work shows, that there in robots exist the same connection between cost of trans- port and the weight of the robots as is true for animals.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Jørgen Christian","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-644249"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["LocoKit","Locomotion","Modular robot","Quadruped","Robot"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy efficiency of robot locomotion increases proportional to weight","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/53142877/FET2011_Preamble.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-644249","ids":["sdu-f83ad37f-e672-42ef-9d01-f260f17aa60f"],"keyword":["LocoKit","Locomotion","Modular Robot","Quadruped","Robot"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-74B52126A8AEB04295548F2265DD6D1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/53142877/FET2011_Preamble.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen Christian","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7360ab40-7502-495e-9745-33ad27e0e1cd","name":"Larsen, Jørgen Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-4741-8290","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"dab546c1-7862-404d-b783-4bdb8a321d52","name":"Støy, Kasper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f83ad37f-e672-42ef-9d01-f260f17aa60f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Energy Efficiency of Robot Locomotion Increases Proportional to Weight","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-644249","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
