{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Bordignon, Mirko","Støy, Kasper","Schultz, Ulrik Pagh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-734326"],"event":{"end":"2011-09-30","place":"San Francisco, us","start":"2011-09-25","title":"2011 IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems<br/>","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generalized programming of modular robots through kinematic configurations","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84455172163","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-734326","identifier":[{"id":"84455172163","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-dfc647ef-610a-4078-aac0-643ff63b07a0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67BDBA096582D0595D34E48332E5FCDA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mirko","key":"bordignonpau","last":"Bordignon","locid":"fc357837-c0e4-44fb-a4bb-63316c2d39ae","name":"Bordignon, Mirko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"dab546c1-7862-404d-b783-4bdb8a321d52","name":"Støy, Kasper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Pagh","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","locid":"79a07bec-ac88-404c-8d6b-c9180214bcc6","name":"Schultz, Ulrik Pagh","orcid":"0000-0003-4119-2689","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iros.2011.6094811","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84455172163"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-dfc647ef-610a-4078-aac0-643ff63b07a0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Generalized programming of modular robots through kinematic configurations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-734326","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Modular robots are mechatronic devices that enable the construction of highly versatile and flexible robotic systems whose mechanical structure can be dynamically modified. The key feature that enables this dynamic modification is the capability of the individual modules to connect to each other in multiple ways and thus generate a number of different mechanical systems, in contrast with the monolithic, fixed structure of conventional robots. The mechatronic flexibility, however, complicates the development of models and programming abstractions for modular robots, since manually describing and enumerating the full set of possible interconnections is tedious and error-prone for real-world robots. In order to allow for a general formulation of spatial abstractions for modular robots and to ensure correct and streamlined generation of code dependent on mechanical properties, we have developed the Modular Mechatronics Modelling Language (M3L). M3L is a domain-specific language, which can model the kinematic structure of individual robot modules and declaratively describe their possible interconnections, rather than requiring the user to enumerate them in their entirety. From this description, the M3L compiler generates the code that is needed to simulate the resulting robots within Webots, a widely used commercial robot simulator, and the software component needed for spatial structure computations by a virtual machine-based runtime system, which we have developed and used for programming physical modular robots.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bordignon, Mirko","Schultz, Ulrik Pagh","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S02-092.86-038351"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Domain specific language","Dynamic Structural Modification","Kinematic Modelling","Mechatronic Flexibility","Modular Robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model based kinematics generation for modular mechatronic toolkits","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/1942788.1868318","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.86-038351","identifier":[{"id":"79951738984","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-97c14047-d531-4a03-8b79-385f0f4377c6","sdu-c3805bac-2549-453f-90a5-c48556f4a336"],"keyword":["Domain-Specific Language","Dynamic Structural Modification","Kinematic Modelling","Mechatronic Flexibility","Modular Robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7BCC57324BD322E88CB39D61864BC0B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/1942788.1868318","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT Univer